# Slide 2 — SafeFlow AI

### “AI-Powered Workflow Recovery Sandbox”

“SafeFlow AI is our attempt to rethink how workflow failures are handled in enterprise applications.

At a high level, SafeFlow combines three major concepts together:

* real-time failure detection,
* AI-powered recovery guidance,
* and isolated sandbox validation.

The workflow starts normally, just like any other enterprise workflow experience.

But when a failure occurs, SafeFlow immediately detects the issue and captures the current workflow context and session state.

From there, the AI assistant analyzes the failure and generates a recommended recovery path using historical defect patterns and contextual workflow information.

Now, this is where our project becomes different from a traditional chatbot assistant.

Most AI assistants stop at recommendations.

They might say:
‘Try changing this field,’
or:
‘This validation commonly fails because of X.’

But the actual user still has to take the risk of applying changes directly against production workflows.

SafeFlow introduces a safe recovery layer.

Instead of blindly retrying in production, users can click a ‘Test Safely’ option which launches an isolated sandbox version of their current workflow session.

Inside that sandbox, users can:

* test modifications,
* rerun validation,
* experiment with recovery options,
* and confirm workflow success safely before touching production.

Once the fix succeeds, the validated changes can then be promoted back into the live workflow session.

So instead of AI only acting as an advisor, SafeFlow creates a full recovery experience.

And that sandbox validation layer is really the core innovation behind our project.”

