# Slide 3 — Demo / User Flow

### “How SafeFlow AI Works”

“Before jumping into the live demo, we wanted to quickly walk through the overall user journey.

The process starts with a user progressing through a normal workflow.

In our case, we focused specifically on a SAMX-style ZIP validation flow because it was one of the examples repeatedly mentioned during the kickoff discussions and gave us a realistic enterprise scenario to model.

Everything begins normally until the workflow encounters a validation failure.

Traditionally, this is where the user experience starts breaking down.

The user may receive a generic error message with little guidance on what actually failed or how to recover.

Instead, SafeFlow immediately detects the issue and launches the AI assistant interface.

The assistant analyzes the failure context and surfaces a recommended explanation and recovery suggestion based on historical defect intelligence.

At this point, the user has two options:

* retry directly in production,
* or launch the SafeFlow recovery sandbox.

When the user clicks ‘Test Safely,’ SafeFlow clones the existing workflow session into an isolated environment.

This is important because the sandbox mirrors the workflow state without impacting the live production flow.

Inside the sandbox, users can safely:

* modify values,
* rerun validation logic,
* test fixes,
* and confirm workflow recovery.

Once validation succeeds, the user can then promote the successful changes back into the live workflow experience.

So instead of escalating the issue into another ticketing cycle, the user resolves the issue directly inside the workflow itself.

At this point we’ll transition into the live demonstration.”

